From 3d8832ff0d9d87dbeadc13205cb1e59723d8da82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UMP <ump@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 83/90] The Java client's first frame runs while the player is
 idle at the title

CLIENT_STARTED, the client's resource reload and the models' start ran on the mirror's first tick, inside the world's join (JourneyMap's CLIENT_STARTED ~2 s, ~3.3 s in all with 184 mods). Horizon now asks for it from the title's frames once the mods' start has ended and no world is opening; Java runs it once on a thread of its own and the first tick waits for it. Started at the same time as a world's opening it only competed with it (tried twice, reverted). HORIZON_EARLY_CLIENT=0 keeps it on the first tick.

UMP player-flow test, 184 mods, 5 s at the title: click->in world 27/27 s (on) vs 28/29 s (off); no title wait: 31 s, as before.
